(0+ rx…)
Match the rxs zero or more times. Greedy by default.
Corresponding string regexp: ‘A*’ (greedy), ‘A*?’ (non-greedy)

(one-or-more rx…) ¶
(1+ rx…)
Match the rxs one or more times. Greedy by default.
Corresponding string regexp: ‘A+’ (greedy), ‘A+?’ (non-greedy)

(zero-or-one rx…) ¶
(optional rx…)
